{%- assign pg_gift_p = all_products['r36s-protective-case-free-gift'] -%}
{%- assign pg_gift_v = pg_gift_p.variants | first -%}
{%- assign pg_gift_was = pg_gift_v.compare_at_price | money -%}
{%- if pg_gift_v.compare_at_price == nil or pg_gift_v.compare_at_price == 0 -%}{%- assign pg_gift_was = '$13.99' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Tune: the drawer's small corrections.

  THE UPSELL TILE IS pg-unlock, NOT nc-cro. Rounds of work here went into
  nc-cro's .nc-rec rows while the tile the owner was pointing at -- "Add a 2nd
  PocketBoy R36" with its SAVE 25% chip and its spare-case tickbox -- is built
  by pg-unlock, under entirely different class names. That is why it never
  changed. Both are styled now; the pg-unlock block is the one that matters on
  the console page.

  NO "YOU SAVED (57%)" ROW. pg-cart-total renders the summary block as
  Subtotal / Extra 10% Off / You saved (n%), and the theme's own Total sits
  right beneath it. Per the owner the saved line comes out: the discount rows
  above it already say what came off, and repeating it as a percentage next to
  the real total is noise at the moment of paying.

  SHIPPING PROTECTION, BIGGER. In the sticky panel pg-drawer shrinks the whole
  box hard -- icon 42px to 28px and its svg 22 to 16, title 14.5 to 12.5px, sub
  12 to 10.5px, price 14.5 to 12.5px -- and it reads as fine print beside the
  checkout button. All five are stepped back up, the words, the icon and the
  price together. The padding stays trimmed because the panel is sticky and
  height added there pushes checkout down.

  THE nc-cro UPSELL ROWS, AND WHY THEY NEVER MOVED EITHER. Every rule for them
  was `#cart .nc-rec-*` -- one id, one class. nc-cro styles the same elements as
  `#cart .nc-recs-panel .nc-rec-*` -- one id, TWO classes -- and it loads last,
  in footer-group, so it won on specificity and on source order. Re-written at
  `#cart#cart#cart`, the same trick nc-cartfix already uses against nc-cro.

  THE TOP OF THE DRAWER: THE WHITE BAND AND THE FAINT RULES. Two hairlines stack
  above the first cart line:

    - pg-drawer's .pg-cart-top is the sticky "Your Cart" header, and it carries
      `border-bottom:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.16)` -- a faint PURPLE rule;
    - nc-cartfix's .nc-drawer-top is the logo + "Free shipping on every order"
      block, `padding:2px 0 14px`, `margin:0 0 8px`, and its own
      `border-bottom:1px solid rgba(15,42,51,.08)` sitting directly under that
      pill -- the second rule, and the band of empty white between them.

  Both borders come off and the block is compressed. .pg-bar's border stays:
  that one outlines the free-shipping progress card, so it reads as a box.

  THE FREE GIFT LINE'S PRICE CORNER, OWNED OUTRIGHT. It should read like every
  other line: struck old price, $0.00, and the percentage under them in the
  bottom-right corner. Two earlier attempts failed for the same reason -- they
  borrowed the theme's own machinery:

    - pg-drawer's pgDeals, which builds .pg-save-chip and the struck price,
      returns early on any row whose link contains 'free-gift', so neither is
      ever created on that line;
    - pg-drawer then hides .pg-save-chip on it as well;
    - pg-chips DOES reach the row, but writes the word FREE into a chip it
      finds and its setWas() only rewrites a struck element it finds -- neither
      creates one;
    - and borrowing .nc-lsave meant depending on nc-cro to build the cell,
      pg-chips to fill it, and pg-drawer's :has() rules to agree about it.

  Three owners for one corner, and the struck price never appeared. So the cell
  is built here under classes nothing else in the theme writes or hides --
  .pg-gift-cell / .pg-gift-was / .pg-gift-now / .pg-gift-off -- and the theme's
  own price node and any .nc-lsave on that line are hidden, so the corner can
  never show two. One owner, nothing to negotiate.

  THE FREE GIFT PILL WAS IN THE WRONG GRID CELL. This was asked for many times
  and answered wrongly every time, because the wrong thing was being measured.
  Measured properly at 390px against the drawer's own grid: the title's box
  starts at x=13, the pill's at x=285 -- 272px to its right, hard against the
  price column. It was never a question of where the words sit INSIDE the pill;
  the pill was not under the title at all.

  pg-drawer places it with `grid-area:sv;justify-self:start` inside
  `"nm nm" "vr vr" "sv sv" "qt pr"`. Anything that perturbs that placement
  auto-flows the pill into the next free cell -- the right-hand `auto` column.
  The placement is now restated at four ids: full row, start-aligned, no auto
  margin. The inline geometry ftFix owns (width, text-indent) is still taken
  back in script, since inline !important cannot be beaten from a stylesheet.

  THE SPARE CASE LINE, SLIGHTLY BIGGER. Its title steps from the drawer's
  16.5px/700 to 17.5px/800, scoped to that product's rows and excluding the gift
  line, which is deliberately the thinner module.

  WHY pg-gift-fix IS GONE. It added the free case itself. So does pg-giftguard,
  which already owned that job — pg-drawer's own giftSync was disabled in favour
  of it, with a comment saying exactly why: "re-enabling this add would mean TWO
  owners racing to add the same gift and a cart that intermittently holds two of
  them. One owner." pg-gift-fix made a third owner, on its own clock, each
  refreshing the drawer after its own add. That is the cart glitching, and the
  second case. Deleted, not patched.
{%- endcomment -%}
