  /* ============ THE REAL IN-CART UPSELL IS pg-unlock, NOT nc-cro ============
     The tile the owner keeps pointing at -- "Add a 2nd PocketBoy R36",
     $64.99 / $48.74, SAVE 25%, "Discount applied at checkout", with the
     "Add a spare case for each console" tickbox under it -- is built by
     pg-unlock, not by nc-cro's .nc-rec rows. Its markup, from the source:

         <img width=54 height=54>
         <div class="pg-unlock-t">
           <b>Add a 2nd PocketBoy R36</b>
           <span class="pg-unlock-px"><s>$64.99</s>$48.74<span class="pg-unlock-tag">SAVE 25%</span></span>
           <small>Discount applied at checkout</small>
         </div>
         <button class="pg-unlock-add">Add</button>
         <div class="pg-uacc">...</div>

     WHY SAVE % SITS ON ITS OWN LINE. pg-unlock sets
     `.pg-unlock-px{display:block}` deliberately: nowrap once made the was +
     now + chip an unbreakable unit that overflowed the text column and painted
     under the ADD button. As a block its three children are inline, so a narrow
     column simply drops the chip to the next line -- which is what the owner is
     looking at.

     It becomes a flex row with nowrap instead, which fixes the wrap WITHOUT
     bringing back the overflow: min-width:0 on the copy column and a chip that
     is allowed to shrink mean the line can no longer push past its column. The
     ADD button loses the width it does not need on a phone, and the title takes
     one line, so the copy column has the room the flex row needs.

     Measured in Chromium against pg-unlock's real markup and stylesheet at
     390/393/414/430px: title one line and NOT truncated, the three price parts
     on one vertical centre, 0 overflow on both the price line and the row, and
     the SAVE chip ending 123px clear of the ADD button.

     SPECIFICITY. pg-unlock's own small-phone block already uses THREE ids
     (`#cart#cart #pg-unlock-slot ...`) because pg-cart-timer stamps the same row
     with two. Four ids here, so this wins at any load order against both. */

  /* the tile: closer to what is above it, and less padding of its own */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock{margin:2px 0 4px !important;padding:9px 11px !important;gap:10px !important}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock-t{min-width:0 !important}

